        <p>"skirts" af the blouse and the sleeves are racked on to Hat yoke, and are laid in a series of deep tucks horizontally. The long cuffs should be carried out in such a manner as to match the yoke. A folded belt, of the same crêpe-de-chine as the blouse, is prettily finished with a double row of tiny rosettes placed down the front. This blouse need not be lined if it is worn over a well-boned silk slip.</p>
        <p>GOSSIP.</p>
        <p>There hangs over the average ladies' club, says a contemporary, an atmosphere of veiled hostility and suspicion, brought about by the unfriendly attitude of the members to one another.</p>
        <p>It is a remarkable fact that there are only four statues in the United Kingdom erected to women other than royalties. These are to Sister Dora the Walsall nurse, to Mrs. Siddons, to Flora Macdonald, and one at Dunoon erected in memory of Burns's "Highland Mary." "Not smart" is the verdict that kills nowadays; and, in truth, if we do not feel smart, says Coming Modes, we are no good. Competition is keen, and anything calculated to lower our standard of self is not to be thought of. Eat well if you can; dress well you must,</p>
        <p>INDOOR GOWN.</p>
        <p>That our gowns must be of ample fulness is, a foregone conclusion, but it is also decreed that every woman must, at the same time, present a slim appearance to the world. These two points seem difficult to combine in one gown, but with a little thought the desired effect can be arrived at. For instance, we have here illustrated an indoor gown having tiny pin-head tucks running down the bodice and continuing over the hips in the skirt;</p>
        <p>this arrangement will give height, even though the line of tuckings is broken by the swathed belt. The skirt will, of course, be much gored, and daintily finished with tucks along the hem. The bodice, with its lace collar, opens over a yoke of .the same lace, and the belt is finished with rows of tiny enamel buttons, while the bodice must only pouch very slightly over it. The sleeves are made with two small puffs, reaching to the elbows, while the long, closely-fitting cuffs are laid in pin tucks to match the bodice.</p>
